cuda_kernel modules go to the disk kernel cache like MLX's own JIT kernels (MLX passed
use_disk_cache = false for them), so NVRTC compiles each once per machine instead of once per
process. The module name hashes the generated source, and mlx-serve keys the cache directory by
its MLX build stamp, so a cached module never outlives its source or its headers.

Retires when upstream caches custom kernels on disk. Not reported upstream yet.

diff --git a/mlx/backend/cuda/custom_kernel.cpp b/mlx/backend/cuda/custom_kernel.cpp
index c230656d8..35f725c25 100644
--- a/mlx/backend/cuda/custom_kernel.cpp
+++ b/mlx/backend/cuda/custom_kernel.cpp
@@ -319,7 +319,8 @@ void CustomKernel::eval_gpu(
         return std::make_tuple(
             is_precompiled_, source_, std::vector{kernel_name});
       },
-      false);
+      // Cached on disk too: the module name hashes the generated source.
+      true);
 
   // Make the arguments
   cu::KernelArgs args;
